# ADR-0001: Project genesis

- **Status:** Accepted
- **Date:** @@DATE@@
- **Deciders:** blamechris
- **Supersedes:** none

## Context

`blamechris/@@NAME@@` is a new repository. The fleet starts every new repository from
the Fleet Project Genesis Standard v1, so that settings, ruleset, labels, doctrine files,
skills and CI are in place before the first line of feature code.

## Options

1. Start from the standard with `/project-genesis` (this ADR).
2. Start ad hoc and back-port later, which is how drift between fleet repos accumulated.

## Decision

Created with `/project-genesis` to Standard v1:

| Choice | Value |
|---|---|
| Visibility | @@VISIBILITY@@ |
| Stack overlays | @@OVERLAYS@@ |
| Modules | @@MODULES@@ |
| App ID | @@APP_ID@@ |
| Self-merge posture | @@POSTURE@@ |
| Waivers | none |

@@CREDITS_POSTURE@@

## Consequences

- `main` accepts changes only through squash-merged PRs gated on `ci-gate`; the ruleset
  has no bypass actors.
- The app ID above is reserved now. Once an app is published under it, it can never change.
- Deviations from the standard are recorded as a `waivers:` entry in
  `.claude/skill-profile.md` plus an ADR, and audit reports them WAIVED.

